Subject: [PATCH] mtk-mdp3: match the MT8183 SCP firmware ABI, fix unload

The MT8183 SCP firmware in linux-firmware (kukui_scp_v2.0.13324) speaks
the ChromeOS 5.10 MDP3 ABI, not the one upstream was written against
(a prebuild that was never published). Every frame failed with
"VPU MDP failure:-22" and the SCP logged "MDP_FRAME Error Data".

- img_output carries a u64 pqid and img_ipi_frameparam ends with
  frame_change. Without pqid the firmware reads config_data 32 bytes
  late, finds 0 and rejects the frame.
- mdp_sm_mt8183.h is the ChromeOS 5.10 config layout: every field is
  32 bits and the component union holds all PQ blocks. Checked against
  a config dumped from the firmware: num_components, the component
  types and num_subfrms land where these structs put them.
- The third img_mux field is the MMSYS instance (vpp_id), not a GCE
  subsys. Writing it as a subsys sent the mux setup to 0x1300xxxx and
  RDMA0 never reached EOF. Resolve it through the MMSYS node's
  mediatek,gce-client-reg.

Unloading the module was also broken:

- mdp_remove() never unregistered the video node, so the mailbox
  channels stayed taken and the next probe failed with -EBUSY.
- The release path disabled runtime PM on pdev a second time. On MT8183
  pdev is RDMA0, so after one reload it could not be powered (-EACCES).
- mdp_comp_destroy() freed components with devm_kfree() on the
  component device, but they are allocated on pdev.

Tested on krane with V4L2 m2m: ARGB32 rotated 0/90/180/270 degrees is
bit-exact. 1920x930 takes 6.3 ms, 1920x1200 7.5 ms. ABGR32 in and out
swaps R and B, so callers that only rotate should use ARGB32 for any
4-byte format.

--- a/drivers/media/platform/mediatek/mdp3/mtk-mdp3-core.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/mediatek/mdp3/mtk-mdp3-core.c
@@ -135,8 +135,6 @@
 	destroy_workqueue(mdp->job_wq);
 	destroy_workqueue(mdp->clock_wq);
 
-	pm_runtime_disable(&mdp->pdev->dev);
-
 	vb2_dma_contig_clear_max_seg_size(&mdp->pdev->dev);
 
 	mdp_comp_destroy(mdp);
@@ -367,10 +365,18 @@
 static void mdp_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct mdp_dev *mdp = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
+	struct video_device *vdev = mdp->m2m_vdev;
 
 	v4l2_device_unregister(&mdp->v4l2_dev);
-
 	dev_dbg(&pdev->dev, "%s driver unloaded\n", pdev->name);
+
+	/*
+	 * The video node's release callback frees the mailbox channels, the
+	 * SCP reference and mdp itself. Without this the node outlives the
+	 * module and the next probe finds the GCE channels still taken.
+	 */
+	if (vdev)
+		video_unregister_device(vdev);
 }
 
 static int __maybe_unused mdp_suspend(struct device *dev)
